<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson says signs China contract.</title>
<headline>Ericsson says signs China contract.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Monday it signed a DCS 1800 network contract with Shanghai Post &amp; Telecommunication Adminstration in China.  </p>
<p>The DCS 1800 network is a personal communication system based on the global system for mobile communications (GSM), the company said in a statement, without disclosing the value of the order.</p>
<p>This is the first contract for a stand-alone DCS 1800 in China, Ericsson said.</p>
<p>The network will have a capacity of 126,000 subscribers, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
